# Allow the block editor's canvas to load these faces.
#
# `add_editor_style()` (functions.php) inlines main.css into the editor canvas, and that canvas is an
# `about:srcdoc` iframe whose origin is `null`. Font fetches are always CORS-mode, so the absolute
# @font-face URLs in this directory were blocked and the canvas fell back to system fonts — the
# Access-Control-Allow-Origin errors an editor sees in the console. The front end is same-origin and was
# never affected.
#
# Scoped to font files in this directory only. Fonts carry no credentials and no user data, and these
# are open-licensed faces (see LICENSE-Cairo.txt / LICENSE-Open-Sans.txt), so `*` grants nothing that
# fetching the stylesheet would not. Wrapped in <IfModule> so a host without mod_headers keeps today's
# behaviour instead of erroring.
<IfModule mod_headers.c>
	<FilesMatch "\.(woff2?|ttf|otf|eot)$">
		Header set Access-Control-Allow-Origin "*"
	</FilesMatch>
</IfModule>
